orization (customer vs staff vs admin)"}],"id":"61-api-areas","readingChosen":"Each listed API area corresponds to actual callable endpoints backing the UI behaviours described elsewhere; listed as required backend capability, not new behaviour beyond what's described in other sections."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Nightly job imports ERP stock CSV automatically"},{"kind":"happy","text":"Email sending is processed by a background job/queue rather than blocking user requests"},{"kind":"happy","text":"Invoice generation runs automatically upon order delivery (as a background process)"},{"kind":"happy","text":"A scheduled job updates invoices to Overdue status based on rules"},{"kind":"happy","text":"A scheduled job removes/expires old password-reset tokens so they can no longer be used"},{"kind":"happy","text":"A scheduled job expires stale invitations so they can no longer be accepted"},{"kind":"error","text":"If a scheduled job fails, it does not silently retry forever or corrupt data; failure is logged (ties to audit/ERP import failure event)"}],"id":"62-background-jobs","readingChosen":"Each listed task runs automatically on a schedule/trigger without manual staff action, producing observable side effects (stock updated, emails sent, invoices created, tokens cleaned)."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Product images are stored and retrievable for display in catalogue/product detail"},{"kind":"happy","text":"Invoice PDFs are stored and retrievable for customer/staff download"},{"kind":"data","text":"ERP CSV files and generated report files may also be stored, pending confirmation"}],"id":"63-file-storage","readingChosen":"System needs durable file storage for product images and invoice PDFs at minimum, with CSV/report storage as 'potential' (lower certainty) needs."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer can download a PDF of any of their invoices"},{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff can download/view PDF of any invoice within their access"},{"kind":"error","text":"If PDF generation fails, user sees a friendly error rather than a broken download"},{"kind":"data","text":"Template branding, tax info, numbering scheme are open points pending clarification"}],"id":"64-pdf-generation","readingChosen":"Portal generates an invoice PDF (format/branding TBD) and makes it downloadable; exact template fidelity is unresolved."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"error","text":"Import rejects/flags a file missing required headers"},{"kind":"error","text":"Import rejects/flags rows referencing unknown product codes, reporting them"},{"kind":"error","text":"Import rejects/flags rows with non-numeric quantities"},{"kind":"error","text":"Import rejects/flags invalid negative quantities (unless explicitly allowed)"},{"kind":"error","text":"Import detects and reports duplicate product identifiers within the file"},{"kind":"error","text":"Import rejects/flags an empty file"},{"kind":"data","text":"Each import run produces a result summary: records received, records processed successfully, records rejected, and error details"}],"id":"65-csv-import-requirements","readingChosen":"The nightly ERP CSV import performs all listed validations before/while processing, rejecting invalid rows/files and reporting a structured result."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"Exported CSVs include a header row with consistent column names"},{"kind":"data","text":"Dates/times in exports use a single consistent format across all exports"},{"kind":"data","text":"Numbers in exports use a single consistent format (e.g. decimal separator) across all exports"},{"kind":"permission","text":"Only authorized users (per report/data access rules) can download export files"}],"id":"66-csv-export-requirements","readingChosen":"All CSV exports (reports etc.) across the system follow a consistent formatting standard and are access-controlled."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"permission","text":"Customer users only ever see their own company's data (orders, invoices, pricing, etc.)"},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer product pricing is derived from their assigned price list, not a global price"},{"kind":"happy","text":"Stock quantities shown come only from the nightly ERP CSV import"},{"kind":"error","text":"No code path writes stock updates back to the ERP"},{"kind":"happy","text":"Stock import happens nightly on a schedule"},{"kind":"happy","text":"Earliest delivery date is computed based on 14:00 cutoff rule relative to order submission time"},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer can repeat a previous order to quickly recreate a basket"},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer can save and reuse named basket templates"},{"kind":"error","text":"Customer cancellation is blocked once order is Confirmed or later"},{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff can edit order contents while order is pre-Confirmed"},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer receives notification email when order is confirmed"},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer receives notification email when order is out for delivery"},{"kind":"happy","text":"Invoice is created automatically at Delivered status, not before"},{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff can manually mark invoices as paid"},{"kind":"error","text":"Deactivating a user does not remove their historical order/invoice records"},{"kind":"data","text":"Order and invoice records are retained at least 7 years"},{"kind":"error","text":"No online payment capture functionality is built"},{"kind":"error","text":"No native mobile app is built"},{"kind":"error","text":"No delivery route planning functionality is built"},{"kind":"error","text":"No returns/credit-note functionality is built"}],"id":"67-business-rules-summary","readingChosen":"These 20 rules are enforced as hard constraints throughout the system (cross-cutting, restating/binding behaviours already described elsewhere)."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"error","text":"System does not implement online card payment processing"},{"kind":"error","text":"System does not provide a native iOS or Android application"},{"kind":"error","text":"System does not provide multi-language/localization support"},{"kind":"error","text":"System does not implement delivery route planning or driver route optimization"},{"kind":"error","text":"System does not implement returns management or credit notes"},{"kind":"error","text":"System does not write inventory data back to the ERP"},{"kind":"error","text":"System does not provide customer self-service returns"},{"kind":"error","text":"System does not provide marketplace functionality (e.g. multi-vendor)"},{"kind":"error","text":"System does not implement promotions, coupons, volume discounts, tiered or contract-specific pricing unless separately approved"}],"id":"68-out-of-scope","readingChosen":"These items are explicitly excluded from phase 1 delivery; any related requests should be flagged as out of scope rather than implemented."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"Numerous functional details (self-registration, password policy, MFA, SSO, lockout behaviour, address creation rules, category structure, product attributes/variants, vehicle data source, tax treatment, discounts, stock semantics, backordering, delivery slots/zones, invoice numbering/VAT, payment recording, email provider specifics, hosting/environments, audit retention, report revenue definition) remain undefined and must be resolved or assumed explicitly before implementation"}],"id":"69-open-questions","readingChosen":"These are unresolved requirements; no behaviour is specified until answered — flagged as assumptions/risks rather than implemented features."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Code can be run/deployed in local development, dev/test, staging/UAT, and production environments distinctly"},{"kind":"data","text":"Exact deployment/promotion strategy between environments is unresolved pending clarification"}],"id":"70-environments","readingChosen":"Four environments (local, dev/test, staging/UAT, production) must exist as part of delivery, with deployment pipeline between them."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Tests verify successful login, invalid login, account lockout, password reset, invitation acceptance, and deactivated-account login attempts behave correctly"},{"kind":"happy","text":"Tests verify customer isolation, staff access, admin access, and rejection of unauthorized API access"},{"kind":"happy","text":"Tests verify catalogue listing, search, category filtering, vehicle compatibility, retired product handling, and product image display"},{"kind":"happy","text":"Tests verify correct price list application, price change handling, preservation of price on existing orders, and pricing customer isolation"},{"kind":"happy","text":"Tests verify valid/invalid stock imports, duplicate/unknown product handling, out-of-stock and low-stock behaviour"},{"kind":"happy","text":"Tests verify basket add/remove/update, quantity validation, delivery-date rule computation, address selection, order submission, and duplicate submission prevention"},{"kind":"happy","text":"Tests verify order creation, confirmation, staff editing, customer cancellation, reordering, status transitions, and triggered email notifications"},{"kind":"happy","text":"Tests verify automatic invoice creation, PDF generation, invoice visibility rules, payment status, and marking paid"},{"kind":"happy","text":"Tests verify report date filtering, correct totals, and CSV export correctness"}],"id":"71-testing-requirements","readingChosen":"Automated/manual test coverage must exist for each listed scenario across the listed functional areas before release."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"error","text":"Customer A requesting orders never receives Customer B's orders, even via direct ID/URL manipulation in API calls"},{"kind":"happy","text":"Product price shown to Customer A reflects Price List A assigned to them"},{"kind":"data","text":"Orders retain the price at time of placement even if the customer's price list changes afterward"},{"kind":"happy","text":"Order submitted before 14:00 on a working day gets next working day as earliest delivery date"},{"kind":"happy","text":"Order submitted at/after 14:00 on a working day gets the following working day as earliest delivery date"},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer cancelling a Received order moves it to Cancelled"},{"kind":"error","text":"Customer attempting to cancel a Confirmed order via the portal is blocked"},{"kind":"happy","text":"Order moving to Delivered status (successfully saved) automatically creates an invoice for that order"}],"id":"72-acceptance-criteria","readingChosen":"These are binding, literal acceptance tests to be implemented exactly as written (customer isolation, pricing snapshot, 14:00 cutoff, cancellation window, auto invoice creation)."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"No additional system behaviour beyond phased grouping of previously described features (foundation, catalogue, ordering, staff ops, invoicing, administration, integrations/reporting, QA/production)"}],"id":"73-suggested-delivery-phases","readingChosen":"This is a planning/sequencing artifact, not a behavioural requirement in itself — no new system behaviour beyond what's described in other sections."}]},{"spans":[{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff selects a date range and views Orders per Day report showing date, order count, and order value per day within range."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff views Top Products report showing product name, quantity sold, and revenue for the selected range."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff views Revenue per Customer report showing customer name, number of orders, and revenue for the selected range."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Only staff/admin roles can access report screens; customer users cannot view reports."},{"kind":"error","text":"If no orders exist in the range, each report shows zero/empty rows rather than erroring."},{"kind":"data","text":"Report revenue calculation includes/excludes cancelled orders and tax per a defined rule (currently undefined, flagged as open point)."}],"id":"39-reporting","readingChosen":"Staff (not customers) can access three required reports (Orders per Day, Top Products, Revenue per Customer) filtered by a selected date range."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"User enters start date and end date and report results update to only include records within that inclusive range."},{"kind":"error","text":"If start date is after end date, system shows a validation error and does not run the report."},{"kind":"error","text":"If no date range is supplied, system applies a default range or prompts the user (open point, default behaviour to be defined)."}],"id":"40-report-filters","readingChosen":"Start/end date filters are mandatory for all reports; customer/product/category filters are optional/not required in phase 1."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff clicks 'Export CSV' on a report and downloads a CSV file containing the same rows/columns shown on screen for the current filter."},{"kind":"data","text":"CSV filename reflects report type and date range."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Only staff with report access can trigger export."},{"kind":"error","text":"Exporting an empty report (no results) still produces a valid CSV with header row only."}],"id":"41-report-export","readingChosen":"Each of the three reports can be exported as CSV matching the on-screen data for the currently applied filters."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"System writes an audit log entry (actor, action type, target entity, timestamp) whenever any listed event occurs: user invited/deactivated, product created/changed/retired, price changed, customer price list changed, order created/amended/confirmed/cancelled/status changed, invoice created/marked paid, ERP import succeeded/failed."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Only admin (and possibly staff) can view the Audit History screen; customers cannot."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Admin views audit history list, filterable/sortable by date, user, or action type."},{"kind":"error","text":"If an audited action fails before completion, no audit log entry for success is written (only failure events like ERP import failed)."}],"id":"42-audit-history","readingChosen":"Every listed event type is recorded as an immutable audit log entry visible to authorized staff/admin."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Inviting a user sends an invitation email with a link to set up the account."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Requesting password reset sends an email with a reset link."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Confirming an order sends an order confirmation email to the customer."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Amending an order sends an order amendment email to the customer."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Marking an order out for delivery sends a notification email to the customer."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Cancelling/rejecting an order sends a cancellation/rejection email where applicable."},{"kind":"error","text":"If email sending fails, the triggering action (e.g. order confirmation) still completes and failure is logged rather than blocking the user."}],"id":"43-notifications","readingChosen":"Each listed event automatically triggers a system email to the relevant recipient via the configured email provider."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"Outgoing emails are sent using the client's configured provider credentials (SMTP or API) once determined."},{"kind":"data","text":"Sender and reply-to addresses are configurable rather than hard-coded."},{"kind":"error","text":"Provider/auth/template/bounce-handling specifics remain open and not yet implemented behaviours."}],"id":"44-email-provider","readingChosen":"The application integrates with a yet-undetermined client email provider; concrete configuration is deferred."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Scheduled nightly job reads the ERP CSV file and updates stock quantities for matched products."},{"kind":"data","text":"Portal never writes stock changes or inventory transactions back to the ERP system."},{"kind":"error","text":"If the file cannot be read/parsed, the import fails and an error/notification is generated (mechanism open)."},{"kind":"data","text":"Exact file delivery, format, product identifier, frequency, and retention of historical imports are open points not yet defined."}],"id":"45-erp-stock-integration","readingChosen":"A nightly scheduled job reads a CSV file supplied by the ERP, imports stock quantities into the portal, and never writes back to the ERP."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"Order and invoice records are retained in the system for a minimum of 7 years from creation."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Authorized users can still view historical orders/invoices tied to a deactivated/deleted user."},{"kind":"error","text":"Deleting a user account does not delete or cascade-delete that user's associated order/invoice records."}],"id":"46-data-retention","readingChosen":"Orders and invoices must be stored for at least 7 years and remain visible to users with appropriate permission even after the acting user is deleted."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Buyer-facing pages (catalogue, basket, checkout, etc.) are fully usable with touch input on small mobile screens."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Same pages adapt layout correctly on tablet and desktop viewports."},{"kind":"error","text":"Exact supported browser/device matrix is undefined; no specific legacy browser support guaranteed."}],"id":"47-responsive-design","readingChosen":"All customer and staff pages must render and function correctly on mobile, tablet, and desktop, with mobile given priority for buyer screens."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Catalogue browsing, search, product detail, basket operations, checkout, order history, and staff order queue respond within a reasonable time under expected concurrent load."},{"kind":"data","text":"No explicit SLA/response-time thresholds are defined yet (open point)."}],"id":"48-performance","readingChosen":"The system must handle expected load (300 buyers, 15 staff, 150 orders/day) with reasonable response times on key workflows, though no numeric targets are fixed."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"User passwords are stored hashed (e.g. bcrypt), never in plaintext."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Each API endpoint enforces role-based authorization server-side (customer/staff/admin)."},{"kind":"error","text":"Unauthenticated or unauthorized API requests are rejected with 401/403 responses."},{"kind":"happy","text":"File uploads are validated for type/size before acceptance; invalid files are rejected."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Password-reset tokens are single-use, time-limited, and cryptographically secure."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Production traffic is served only over HTTPS."},{"kind":"error","text":"Input validation rejects malformed/malicious input (e.g. XSS, SQL injection attempts) with safe error responses."}],"id":"49-security","readingChosen":"Standard web security controls are implemented application-wide: secure auth, hashed passwords, RBAC, tenant isolation, secure sessions, API protection, input/file validation, common-vulnerability protection, secure reset tokens, HTTPS in prod."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer user requesting their own orders/invoices/addresses/pricing/users/account info receives only their own company's data."},{"kind":"error","text":"Customer user attempting to access another customer's data (e.g. by changing an ID in the URL/API) receives a 403/404, not the data."},{"kind":"data","text":"Authorization checks are enforced in backend API logic, not only hidden/disabled in the UI."}],"id":"50-data-isolation","readingChosen":"Server-side authorization strictly prevents any customer user from accessing another customer's orders, invoices, addresses, pricing, users, or account info, regardless of frontend state."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"All interactive elements are reachable and operable via keyboard alone."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Form fields have associated labels and validation messages are announced/readable by screen readers."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Text and UI elements meet readable contrast levels."},{"kind":"data","text":"Specific compliance target (e.g. WCAG 2.1 AA) is not fixed (open point)."}],"id":"51-accessibility","readingChosen":"The portal is designed following accessible practices (keyboard nav, labels, contrast, screen-reader structure) without committing to a specific WCAG conformance level."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"error","text":"Invalid login shows a generic 'invalid credentials' message, not which field was wrong."},{"kind":"error","text":"Expired password-reset link shows a message prompting the user to request a new one."},{"kind":"error","text":"Attempting to order a product no longer available shows a friendly 'no longer available' message."},{"kind":"error","text":"Stock import failure, failed order submission, email delivery failure, invalid CSV, and missing product all produce user-friendly messages without exposing stack traces/sensitive info."},{"kind":"error","text":"Session expiration redirects user to sign-in with a message, preserving no sensitive cached data."}],"id":"52-error-handling","readingChosen":"User-facing errors across the listed scenarios show friendly messages, never raw stack traces or internal details."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Search with no matches shows 'no results' empty state with suggestion to adjust search."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Empty basket shows an empty-basket message with a call to browse catalogue."},{"kind":"happy","text":"No orders/invoices/templates/report results show respective friendly empty-state messaging instead of blank tables."}],"id":"53-empty-states","readingChosen":"Each listed list/search view shows a dedicated empty-state message/UI when there is no data, rather than a blank screen."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Catalogue, search, product detail, basket updates, checkout, order submission, invoice generation/download, reports, and staff queues each display a loading indicator while processing, then replace it with results or an error."}],"id":"54-loading-states","readingChosen":"Each listed async operation/screen shows a visible loading indicator (spinner/skeleton) while data is fetched."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer can navigate to and use each of: sign in, forgot password, reset password, catalogue, product detail, vehicle search, basket, checkout, order confirmation, my orders, order detail, invoice list, invoice detail, saved basket templates, account/company details, delivery addresses."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Unauthenticated users can only access sign-in/forgot/reset password screens, not authenticated customer screens."}],"id":"55-main-customer-screens","readingChosen":"Each of the 16 listed customer screens must exist as a distinct, navigable page in the portal."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff can navigate to and use each of: staff sign in, dashboard, order queue, order detail/editor, customer list, customer detail, customer orders, customer invoices, delivery export, reports, invoice management."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Customer users cannot access any staff screen URLs even directly."}],"id":"56-main-staff-screens","readingChosen":"Each of the 11 listed staff screens must exist and be accessible only to staff/admin roles."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Admin can navigate to and use each of: admin dashboard, users, user detail, customers, customer detail, products, product editor, categories, vehicle compatibility, price lists, price list editor, system/import status, audit history."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Staff (non-admin) and customer users are blocked from admin screens/routes."}],"id":"57-main-admin-screens","readingChosen":"Each of the 13 listed admin screens must exist and be restricted to admin role only."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"New order is created with status Received, and progresses through Confirmed, Picking, Out for Delivery, Delivered in sequence as staff update status."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Delivered status triggers automatic invoice creation."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer can cancel an order only while it is in Received status, transitioning it to Cancelled."},{"kind":"error","text":"Attempting to cancel an order once it is Confirmed or later is rejected by the system."},{"kind":"data","text":"Staff-initiated rejection/cancellation at other stages follows separate business rules (not fully specified)."}],"id":"58-order-lifecycle","readingChosen":"Orders move through a fixed sequence of statuses (Received→Confirmed→Picking→Out for Delivery→Delivered→Invoice Created), with cancellation only allowed pre-confirmation."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Marking an order Delivered automatically creates an invoice with status Unpaid."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff can mark an invoice as Paid."},{"kind":"data","text":"Invoice transitions to Overdue based on rules not yet defined (open point)."}],"id":"59-invoice-lifecycle","readingChosen":"An invoice is auto-created when an order is marked Delivered, starting as Unpaid, and can transition to Paid or Overdue."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"System's underlying data model conceptually includes entities such as User, Role, Customer, Product, Order, Invoice, AuditLog, EmailNotification, etc., to support all described behaviours."}],"id":"60-core-data-entities","readingChosen":"This is a conceptual data model list guiding implementation, not literal schema behaviours — no direct observable behaviour required."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Authentication APIs support sign in, sign out, password reset, invitation acceptance, and session/account status checks."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Catalogue APIs return products, categories, product details, search results, and vehicle compatibility data."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Basket APIs support get/add/update/remove/clear operations scoped to the authenticated customer's basket."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Checkout APIs validate basket contents, return delivery options, and submit orders."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Order APIs provide customer and staff order lists/detail, repeat order, cancel, staff edit/confirm/reject/status update, and staff-created orders."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Invoice APIs provide list, detail, PDF download, and mark-paid actions."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Administration APIs (users, customers, products, categories, price lists, vehicle compatibility, imports, audit logs) are restricted to admin role."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Report APIs return orders-per-day, top-products, revenue-by-customer data and CSV exports."}],"id":"61-api-areas","readingChosen":"Backend exposes API endpoints grouped by these functional areas, each requiring appropriate auth/role enforcement."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Nightly job automatically imports ERP stock CSV without manual intervention."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Emails are sent asynchronously via a background job/queue rather than blocking the triggering request."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Invoice generation runs automatically as a background process when an order is delivered."},{"kind":"happy","text":"A scheduled job updates invoices to Overdue status based on defined rules."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Expired password-reset tokens and stale invitations are automatically cleaned up/expired by a scheduled job."}],"id":"62-background-jobs","readingChosen":"Scheduled/background jobs run automatically for the listed maintenance tasks without manual staff triggering."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Uploaded product images are stored and retrievable for display on catalogue/product pages."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Generated invoice PDFs are stored and retrievable for customer/staff download."},{"kind":"data","text":"ERP CSV files and generated report files may also be persisted (provider/location open point)."}],"id":"63-file-storage","readingChosen":"The system persists uploaded/generated files (product images, invoice PDFs, ERP CSVs, report files) in a durable storage location accessible to authorized features."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer can download a PDF of any of their invoices from the invoice detail screen."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff can download/view invoice PDFs for any customer's invoice."},{"kind":"error","text":"If PDF generation fails, user sees a friendly error rather than a broken download, and can retry."},{"kind":"data","text":"Template, branding, tax info, and numbering scheme are unresolved open points."}],"id":"64-pdf-generation","readingChosen":"Each created invoice has a corresponding PDF that customers and staff can download; exact template/branding specifics are open."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Import validates required headers exist before processing; aborts with error if missing."},{"kind":"error","text":"Rows with non-numeric quantities are rejected and reported, not applied."},{"kind":"error","text":"Rows with invalid negative quantities are rejected unless explicitly supported."},{"kind":"error","text":"Duplicate product identifiers within the file are detected and reported as errors."},{"kind":"error","text":"Unknown product identifiers (not matching any portal product) are reported as errors, not silently ignored."},{"kind":"error","text":"An empty file is rejected with an error rather than clearing all stock."},{"kind":"data","text":"After each import, system records counts of records received, processed successfully, rejected, plus error details, accessible via System/Import status screen."}],"id":"65-csv-import-requirements","readingChosen":"The nightly ERP CSV import performs listed validations before applying stock changes, and reports results, rejecting invalid rows while continuing with valid ones."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Every CSV export includes a header row with consistent, human-readable column names."},{"kind":"data","text":"Dates/times in exports use one consistent format; numbers use one consistent format (e.g. decimal separators) across all exports."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Only authorized users (role-appropriate) can trigger/download a given CSV export; unauthorized requests are rejected."}],"id":"66-csv-export-requirements","readingChosen":"All CSV exports across the system follow consistent formatting standards and are access-controlled."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"permission","text":"Customer users' data queries (orders, invoices, etc.) are always scoped to their own company only."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Product prices shown/applied to a customer are derived from that customer's assigned price list."},{"kind":"data","text":"Stock values displayed come solely from the last successful ERP CSV import; portal never pushes stock changes to ERP."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Stock import runs nightly on schedule."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Earliest delivery date offered at checkout is computed from order submission time relative to 14:00 cutoff."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer can trigger 'repeat order' to recreate a basket from a past order."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer can save a named basket template and reuse it later."},{"kind":"error","text":"Customer cancellation action is blocked once an order is Confirmed or later (enforced server-side)."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff can modify order contents only while order is pre-confirmation."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Email notification fires automatically on order confirmation and on out-for-delivery status change."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Invoice is created automatically the moment an order's status becomes Delivered."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff can manually mark any invoice as Paid."},{"kind":"data","text":"Deactivating a user does not remove their historical orders/invoices from reports or records."},{"kind":"data","text":"Order/invoice records persist in the system for at least 7 years."},{"kind":"error","text":"No online payment capture features are present; payment status must be set manually by staff."},{"kind":"error","text":"No native mobile app, delivery route planning, returns, or credit note functionality is present in this phase."}],"id":"67-business-rules-summary","readingChosen":"These 20 rules are enforced as hard constraints system-wide unless later changed."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"error","text":"No card payment flow, native app, multi-language switch, route planning, returns/credit-note screens, ERP write-back, or promotional/coupon/tiered-pricing features exist in the delivered system unless separately approved."}],"id":"68-out-of-scope","readingChosen":"The listed features are explicitly not built in phase 1; any UI referencing them is absent."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"No behaviour is implemented for items still under open question (self-registration, MFA, SSO, lockout policy, variants, substitutes, compatibility data source, volume/promo pricing, backordering, partial fulfillment, delivery slots/zones, VAT, credit notes, payment import, bounce tracking, hosting/provider choice, pen-testing, IP restriction) until clarified."}],"id":"69-open-questions","readingChosen":"These remain unresolved; no committed behaviour yet — flagged for clarification rather than implemented."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"Code can be deployed and run independently in local, dev/test, staging/UAT, and production environments with environment-specific configuration."}],"id":"70-environments","readingChosen":"Four environments (local, dev/test, staging/UAT, production) are provisioned for the project lifecycle."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Test suite verifies successful and invalid login, account lockout, password reset, invitation acceptance, and deactivated-account login rejection."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Test suite verifies customer data isolation, staff/admin access boundaries, and rejection of unauthorized API calls."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Test suite verifies catalogue listing/search/filtering, vehicle compatibility, retired-product exclusion, and image display."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Test suite verifies correct price-list pricing, price change handling, and that historical orders retain original price."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Test suite verifies valid/invalid/duplicate/unknown-product stock imports and out-of-stock/low-stock status display."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Test suite verifies basket operations, quantity validation, delivery-date rule, address selection, order submission, and duplicate-submission prevention."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Test suite verifies order creation, confirmation, staff editing, cancellation, reorder, status transitions, and triggered email notifications."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Test suite verifies automatic invoice creation, PDF generation, invoice visibility rules, payment status, and marking paid."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Test suite verifies report date filtering, correct totals, and CSV export correctness."}],"id":"71-testing-requirements","readingChosen":"Automated/manual test coverage exists for each listed scenario across auth, authorization, catalogue, pricing, stock, basket/checkout, orders, invoices, and reporting."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Buyer from Customer A requesting order list receives only Customer A's orders."},{"kind":"error","text":"Buyer from Customer A modifying an order ID in URL/API to access Customer B's order is denied (not merely hidden in UI)."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer A viewing Product X sees the price from their assigned Price List A."},{"kind":"data","text":"Changing Price List A later does not alter the price shown/charged on Customer A's already-placed orders."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Order submitted before 14:00 on a working day shows next working day as earliest delivery date."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Order submitted at/after 14:00 shows the following working day as earliest delivery date."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Cancelling a Received order changes its status to Cancelled."},{"kind":"error","text":"Attempting to cancel a Confirmed order via the portal is blocked with an appropriate message."},{"kind":"happy","text":"When an order's status is successfully saved as Delivered, an invoice is automatically created for it without manual staff action."}],"id":"72-acceptance-criteria","readingChosen":"These given/when/then examples are binding acceptance tests for isolation, pricing, delivery date, cancellation, and invoice creation."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"Feature delivery is organized into 8 phases (Foundation, Catalogue, Ordering, Staff Ops, Invoicing, Administration, Integrations/Reporting, QA/Production) guiding build order, not end-user-observable behaviour."}],"id":"73-suggested-delivery-phases","readingChosen":"This is a planning/sequencing structure, not itself a functional behaviour — included for completeness only."}]},{"spans":[{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff select a date range and view 'Orders per Day' report showing date, order count, and order value per day."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff view 'Top Products' report showing product, quantity sold, revenue, sorted by revenue or quantity."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff view 'Revenue per Customer' report showing customer, number of orders, revenue."},{"kind":"data","text":"Cancelled orders are excluded from order count/value and revenue totals in all three reports."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Only staff/admin roles can access report screens; customer users get 403/404."},{"kind":"error","text":"No orders in selected range produces an empty report (see Empty States) rather than an error."}],"id":"39-reporting","readingChosen":"Revenue = sum of order value for orders in range, excluding cancelled orders (exact calc rule open)."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff set start date and end date and reports recalculate for that window."},{"kind":"error","text":"If start date is after end date, submission is rejected with a validation message and no report is generated."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Date filters apply identically across all three report types and their exports."}],"id":"40-report-filters","readingChosen":"Only start/end date filtering is implemented in this phase; customer/product/category filters are not built."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff click 'Download CSV' on a report and receive a file containing the same rows/columns as shown on screen."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Only users with report-view permission can trigger the CSV download; unauthorized requests are rejected."},{"kind":"error","text":"If report generation fails, export shows a user-friendly error instead of a broken/empty file."}],"id":"41-report-export","readingChosen":"CSV export mirrors exactly the columns/rows currently displayed on screen for the active filter."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"Each listed event (user invited/deactivated, product created/changed/retired, price changed, customer price list changed, order created/amended/confirmed/cancelled/status changed, invoice created/marked paid, ERP import succeeded/failed) writes an audit log entry with actor, timestamp, action, and target entity."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Only admin users can view the Audit History screen; other roles cannot."},{"kind":"data","text":"Audit log entries cannot be edited or deleted through the application."},{"kind":"error","text":"If writing an audit entry fails, the underlying business action still completes (audit failure does not block the action) and the failure is logged separately."}],"id":"42-audit-history","readingChosen":"Audit entries are created automatically and are append-only (no edit/delete via UI)."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Inviting a user sends an invitation email containing an acceptance link."},{"kind":"happy","text":"A password reset request sends an email with a reset link."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Confirming an order sends the customer an order-confirmation email; amending sends an amendment email; marking out-for-delivery sends a dispatch email; cancelling/rejecting sends a cancellation email where applicable."},{"kind":"error","text":"If the recipient email is missing/invalid, the notification is skipped and an error is recorded, without blocking the triggering action."},{"kind":"error","text":"If the email provider is unreachable, the send is retried/queued or logged as failed rather than crashing the request."}],"id":"43-notifications","readingChosen":"Email send failures are logged but do not block/rollback the underlying action (order confirmation, invite, etc.)."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"Provider credentials/configuration (sender address, auth, etc.) are stored securely and not exposed in UI responses to non-admins."},{"kind":"error","text":"Authentication failure with the provider is logged and surfaced on an admin-visible status area rather than silently failing."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Only admin can view/edit email provider configuration."}],"id":"44-email-provider","readingChosen":"Only admins can see/configure provider credentials; the app sends via whatever provider is configured."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"A scheduled nightly job reads the ERP-supplied CSV and updates stock quantities for matching products."},{"kind":"data","text":"The portal never writes stock data or inventory transactions back to the ERP (no outbound write calls exist)."},{"kind":"error","text":"If the file is missing or malformed, the import fails, previous stock values are left unchanged, and the failure is recorded (visible on System/Import Status screen)."},{"kind":"data","text":"Successful imports immediately update stock visibility for customers and staff on catalogue/product pages."}],"id":"45-erp-stock-integration","readingChosen":"Nightly CSV import updates StockItem records; portal never calls back to ERP."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"Orders and invoices remain stored and queryable for at least 7 years from creation."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Deactivating or deleting a user leaves that user's historical orders/invoices intact and viewable by authorized staff/admin and the owning customer's remaining users."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Historical records are visible according to the viewer's role/customer scope, same as live records."},{"kind":"error","text":"No UI/API path exists to permanently delete order or invoice records."}],"id":"46-data-retention","readingChosen":"Order/invoice records are never hard-deleted; access is controlled by role, not by data existing only for owner."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"All pages render usable, functional layouts at common phone, tablet, and desktop viewport widths."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Buyer-facing flows (catalogue, basket, checkout) are optimized first for mobile usability."},{"kind":"data","text":"No page requires horizontal scrolling or has inaccessible controls at minimum supported mobile width."}],"id":"47-responsive-design","readingChosen":"All required screens (customer, staff, admin) must render usably at mobile widths, not just buyer screens."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"System operates correctly under ~300 buyers, ~15 staff, and up to 150 orders/day without errors or timeouts."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Catalogue browsing, search, product detail, basket operations, checkout, order history, and staff order queue respond within a reasonable time under that load."},{"kind":"error","text":"Under peak load, requests degrade gracefully (e.g., loading indicators, no crashes) rather than failing outright."}],"id":"48-performance","readingChosen":"No numeric SLA is enforced in this phase; system must simply handle stated scale without errors/timeouts."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Passwords are stored hashed (never plaintext) and authentication uses secure, httpOnly/secure session cookies."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Every protected endpoint enforces role-based authorization server-side regardless of UI state."},{"kind":"error","text":"Unauthenticated/unauthorized API calls return 401/403 without leaking data."},{"kind":"data","text":"All inputs (forms and API payloads) are validated/sanitized; file uploads are checked for type/size before acceptance."},{"kind":"data","text":"Production traffic is served only over HTTPS; HTTP requests are redirected or rejected."},{"kind":"data","text":"Password-reset tokens are single-use, time-limited, and cryptographically random."}],"id":"49-security","readingChosen":"Standard controls are baseline requirements applied across all endpoints, not feature-specific."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"A customer user's requests for orders, invoices, addresses, pricing, users, and account info are always scoped server-side to their own customer/company."},{"kind":"error","text":"Modifying an ID in a URL/API request to reference another customer's record returns 403/404, never the other customer's data."},{"kind":"data","text":"Isolation checks occur in backend logic regardless of any frontend hiding of UI elements."}],"id":"50-data-isolation","readingChosen":"Isolation is enforced per authenticated customer/company ID on every server-side query, independent of any client-supplied IDs."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"All interactive elements (menus, forms, buttons) are reachable and operable via keyboard alone."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Form fields have programmatically associated labels and ARIA attributes where needed."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Text and UI elements meet a readable contrast ratio."},{"kind":"error","text":"Validation errors are announced/associated with their field in a way compatible with screen readers, with meaningful (non-generic) messages."},{"kind":"data","text":"Page structure uses semantic HTML (headings, landmarks) for screen-reader navigation."}],"id":"51-accessibility","readingChosen":"Target is WCAG-AA-style practices, though exact compliance level is an open point."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"error","text":"Invalid login attempt shows a generic 'invalid credentials' message, not raw server/auth errors."},{"kind":"error","text":"Expired password-reset link shows a friendly message and offers to request a new one, rather than a stack trace."},{"kind":"error","text":"Attempting to order a product that is no longer available shows a clear message and prevents the submission."},{"kind":"error","text":"Stock import failure, failed order submission, email delivery failure, invalid CSV, and missing product all surface user-friendly messages appropriate to the user's role."},{"kind":"error","text":"Session expiration redirects the user to sign-in with an explanatory message rather than a silent failure or raw error."},{"kind":"data","text":"No raw stack traces, SQL errors, or internal technical details are ever rendered to end users in any scenario."}],"id":"52-error-handling","readingChosen":"For invalid login, a generic 'invalid credentials' message is shown without revealing whether username or password was wrong (security best practice)."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Search with no matches shows a 'no results' empty state with guidance (e.g., adjust search)."},{"kind":"happy","text":"An empty basket shows an 'empty basket' state instead of a blank table."},{"kind":"happy","text":"No orders/invoices/templates/matching products/report results each show a corresponding tailored empty-state message."}],"id":"53-empty-states","readingChosen":"Each listed scenario gets a distinct, friendly empty-state message/illustration rather than a blank or broken screen."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Catalogue, search, product detail, basket updates, checkout, order submission, invoice generation/download, reports, and staff queues each show a visible loading indicator while the operation is in progress."},{"kind":"error","text":"During order submission or checkout processing, the submit control is disabled/hidden to prevent duplicate submissions while loading."}],"id":"54-loading-states","readingChosen":"Loading indicators also disable repeat-submission for actions like order submission/checkout to prevent duplicates."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"All 16 listed customer screens (sign in, forgot/reset password, catalogue, product detail, vehicle search, basket, checkout, order confirmation, my orders, order detail, invoice list/detail, saved templates, account/company details, delivery addresses) exist and are navigable."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Only sign-in, forgot-password, and reset-password are accessible without authentication; all other customer screens require a logged-in customer session."},{"kind":"error","text":"Attempting to access an authenticated customer screen while logged out redirects to sign-in."}],"id":"55-main-customer-screens","readingChosen":"These screens form the customer-portal navigation; unauthenticated users can only reach sign-in/forgot/reset password, all others require login."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"All 11 listed staff screens exist (staff sign in, dashboard, order queue, order detail/editor, customer list/detail/orders/invoices, delivery export, reports, invoice management)."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Only authenticated staff/admin users can access staff screens; customer users attempting access are denied (403/redirect)."}],"id":"56-main-staff-screens","readingChosen":"Staff sign-in is a separate login flow/route from customer sign-in."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"All 13 listed admin screens exist (dashboard, users, customers, products, categories, vehicle compatibility, price lists, import status, audit history, etc.)."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Only admin-role users can access admin screens; staff without admin rights are denied."},{"kind":"data","text":"Audit history screen is view-only, no edit/delete controls present."}],"id":"57-main-admin-screens","readingChosen":"Admin screens require an admin role distinct from general staff role; audit history is read-only."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"New orders are created with status Received and progress through Confirmed, Picking, Out for Delivery, Delivered in sequence."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer can cancel an order only while it is in Received status, transitioning it to Cancelled."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff can confirm, edit, reject, or cancel orders per business rules, including at stages beyond Received."},{"kind":"error","text":"Invalid status transitions (e.g., Delivered back to Picking, or customer cancelling a Confirmed order) are rejected with an explanatory message."},{"kind":"data","text":"Reaching Delivered status automatically creates an invoice for the order."}],"id":"58-order-lifecycle","readingChosen":"Staff cancellation/rejection can occur at more stages than pure customer cancellation (business-rule-driven), beyond just Received."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Invoice is created automatically with status Unpaid when its order is marked Delivered."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff can mark an Unpaid invoice as Paid."},{"kind":"data","text":"A scheduled job transitions Unpaid invoices past their due date to Overdue status automatically."},{"kind":"error","text":"Attempting to mark an already-Paid invoice as Paid again is a no-op or rejected with a message."}],"id":"59-invoice-lifecycle","readingChosen":"Overdue status is set automatically by a scheduled job once a configured due period elapses while invoice remains Unpaid."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"Each business concept (orders, invoices, baskets, price lists, stock, users, audit logs, email notifications, etc.) is persisted with enough structure to support all behaviours described in the other spans."}],"id":"60-core-data-entities","readingChosen":"Treated as conceptual data model support rather than direct user-facing behaviour; main observable effect is that each described business object persists and relates correctly."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"Each listed API area (auth, catalogue, basket, checkout, orders, invoices, administration, reports) exposes endpoints implementing the corresponding behaviours described elsewhere."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Every API endpoint enforces the same role/customer-scoping rules as its corresponding UI screen."}],"id":"61-api-areas","readingChosen":"API behaviour is already covered by the corresponding feature spans; this entry just confirms endpoints exist with consistent auth enforcement."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Nightly ERP stock import job runs on schedule automatically without manual trigger."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Emails are sent via an asynchronous queue so user-facing requests are not blocked by email sending."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Invoice overdue-status update runs periodically and updates all qualifying Unpaid invoices to Overdue."},{"kind":"data","text":"Expired password-reset tokens are periodically cleaned up and become unusable; tokens are also rejected on use after expiry regardless of cleanup timing."},{"kind":"data","text":"Expired/unused invitations are cleaned up or marked expired after their validity window and cannot be accepted afterward."}],"id":"62-background-jobs","readingChosen":"Invoice generation is triggered synchronously on the Delivered status change (per acceptance criteria in span 72); other jobs (import, overdue updates, token/invite cleanup, email sending) run on a schedule/queue."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Product images are stored and served on catalogue/product detail pages."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Generated invoice PDFs are stored and retrievable for download by the owning customer and authorized staff."},{"kind":"data","text":"ERP CSV files received are retained in storage for later reference/debugging."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Stored files are only accessible to users with appropriate permission (e.g., a customer cannot fetch another customer's invoice PDF by guessing a URL)."}],"id":"63-file-storage","readingChosen":"Storage must support retrieval scoped by permission (e.g., invoice PDFs only by the owning customer or staff)."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"When an invoice is created, a PDF is generated containing at minimum line items and totals."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customers can download the PDF for their own invoices; staff can download for any customer's invoice."},{"kind":"error","text":"If PDF generation fails, invoice creation still succeeds but the download shows a friendly error/retry option rather than a broken file."}],"id":"64-pdf-generation","readingChosen":"PDF is generated once per invoice (on creation) and reused for subsequent downloads rather than regenerated each time."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Valid CSV with correct headers, numeric quantities, and known product codes is imported, updating stock for each row."},{"kind":"error","text":"Missing required headers, non-numeric quantities, or an empty file cause the import to fail validation before processing begins."},{"kind":"error","text":"Duplicate product identifiers within the file are detected and reported as rejected rows rather than silently overwriting."},{"kind":"error","text":"Unknown product identifiers are reported as rejected without failing the rest of the import."},{"kind":"data","text":"Each import produces a summary: records received, number processed, number rejected, and per-row error details, visible on the System/Import Status screen."}],"id":"65-csv-import-requirements","readingChosen":"Validation happens before any stock values are written; any rejected rows are excluded without affecting valid rows in the same file."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"All CSV exports include a header row with consistent, human-readable column names."},{"kind":"data","text":"Dates and numbers in exports use a single consistent format across all exports."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Only users authorized to view the underlying report/data can trigger its CSV download; others get 403."}],"id":"66-csv-export-requirements","readingChosen":"Download permission matches the permission required to view the underlying report/data."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"Customer users never see another company's data (ties to span 50)."},{"kind":"data","text":"Product price shown to a customer always derives from that customer's assigned price list."},{"kind":"data","text":"Orders submitted before 14:00 get next working day as earliest delivery; at/after 14:00 get the following working day."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customers can repeat a previous order and can save/name basket templates."},{"kind":"error","text":"Customers can only cancel orders before confirmation; staff can edit orders before confirmation."},{"kind":"data","text":"Online payment, native apps, route planning, and returns/credit notes are not available anywhere in the system."}],"id":"67-business-rules-summary","readingChosen":"These are cross-cutting rules already reflected in other spans; listed here as consolidated acceptance checks."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"error","text":"No UI entry points or API endpoints exist for online card payment, native app-specific APIs, multi-language switching, route optimization, returns, or credit notes."},{"kind":"error","text":"No functionality exists for writing inventory transactions back to the ERP."},{"kind":"data","text":"Advanced pricing features (promotions, coupons, volume/tiered/contract pricing) are absent unless separately approved."}],"id":"68-out-of-scope","readingChosen":"Out-of-scope items have no corresponding UI/API surface at all in this phase, rather than being present but disabled."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"No committed behaviour is implemented purely from this section; items are tracked as open questions pending stakeholder answers, with assumptions noted in the relevant spans above."}],"id":"69-open-questions","readingChosen":"These are unresolved clarification items with no concrete behaviour defined yet; defaults/assumptions used elsewhere in this analysis stand until clarified."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"Separate local, development/test, staging/UAT, and production environments are configured for the application."},{"kind":"data","text":"Production environment enforces HTTPS and restricted access per security requirements (span 49)."}],"id":"70-environments","readingChosen":"At minimum local, dev/test, staging/UAT, and production environments exist with increasing access restriction toward production."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Automated/manual tests exist exercising successful and failed login, lockout, password reset, invitation, and deactivated-account scenarios."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Tests verify customer/staff/admin authorization boundaries and reject unauthorized API access."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Tests cover catalogue/search/pricing/stock scenarios including retired products, out-of-stock items, and low-stock status."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Tests cover basket/checkout flows including duplicate-submission prevention and delivery-date rules."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Tests cover order status transitions, email notification triggers, invoice auto-creation, PDF generation, and payment-status changes."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Tests cover report date filtering, total correctness, and CSV export content."}],"id":"71-testing-requirements","readingChosen":"Testing requirements imply the underlying behaviours (already specified in prior spans) must be verifiable via automated/manual tests; listed here as confirmation that each described behaviour has corresponding test coverage."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"error","text":"A buyer from Customer A requesting orders only ever receives Customer A's orders, including when tampering with IDs in the URL/API (returns no data / error for other customers)."},{"kind":"data","text":"Customer A viewing Product X sees the price from their assigned Price List A; if that price list changes later, previously placed orders still show their original price."},{"kind":"happy","text":"An order submitted before 14:00 on a working day gets next working day as earliest delivery date; submitted at/after 14:00 gets the following working day."},{"kind":"happy","text":"A Received order can be cancelled by the customer, becoming Cancelled."},{"kind":"error","text":"A Confirmed order cannot be cancelled by the customer through the portal; the attempt is rejected with a message."},{"kind":"happy","text":"When an order's delivery status is successfully saved as Delivered, an invoice is automatically created for that order in the same operation."}],"id":"72-acceptance-criteria-examples","readingChosen":"Taken as literal, binding acceptance tests for the described scenarios."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"No new system behaviour is defined by this section beyond what is already specified in the feature-specific spans; it only sequences delivery of those behaviours across phases."}],"id":"73-suggested-delivery-phases","readingChosen":"Purely a planning/roadmap structure with no directly testable system behaviour of its own."}]}]}